FINAL ANSWER:
Two people are still active and have touched this code: **Hiroshi Tanaka** and **Santiago Bartesaghi**. I counted someone as active if they committed in the last 6 months, since 2026-04-23.

- **Hiroshi Tanaka** is the best first reviewer.
  - They wrote `valkey_proxy.rb` and own 100% of it. The commits are "Add Valkey store proxy (#310)" on 2026-09-02 and "ValkeyProxy: add wrap and version check (#318)" on 2026-09-16.
  - They are the only active author with substantive recent work on how proxies are built and wrapped.
  - Their commits use two email addresses, `hiroshi@tanaka.example` and `<email redacted>`. The history tool merged them into one author. I didn't check whether they really are one person.
- **Santiago Bartesaghi** is the second reviewer.
  - They fixed `reset!` for namespaced cache stores (#673, 2024-12-19), which touched `redis_cache_store_proxy.rb`. They own about 12% of that file.
  - Their 2026-08-04 commit, "Autocorrect Style/StringLiterals", was a style autocorrect. It doesn't show deep knowledge of the proxies.
  - Their last commit anywhere in the repo was 2026-09-30. They are the most active contributor over the last 6 months, with 3 commits.

Most of the other store proxy code has no active author left. Five of the six files in `lib/rack/attack/store_proxy/` are owned mostly by inactive authors: `dalli_proxy.rb`, `redis_store_proxy.rb`, `mem_cache_store_proxy.rb`, `redis_proxy.rb` and `redis_cache_store_proxy.rb`. Gonzalo Rodriguez wrote much of that code, but their last commit was in 2021. Only `valkey_proxy.rb` has an active owner.

If your change touches the Redis, Dalli or MemCache proxies, nobody active knows that code well. Ask Hiroshi and Santiago to review it carefully, and run the tests against real backends.

Jonas Keller also committed in the last 6 months, but never touched the store proxy code, so I left them out.

